/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Segment control — liquid-glass WINDOW over a FIXED iridescent foil (Shift ⇄ Day)
   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   No drag. A click switches the mode (kpi_page.js writes --flow-mode-index) and
   flow_glass_control.js runs a SPRING that drives:
     --fg-tx (px slide) · --fg-pp (foil anchor %) · --fg-sx/--fg-sy (squash-stretch)
     --fg-origin (stretch anchor) · --fg-energy (0..1 speed → motion glow)
   All custom props fall back to the index so it still works with JS disabled.

   The thumb (::before) is a WINDOW. Its foil is anchored to the CONTROL: --fg-pp
   counter-tracks --fg-tx, so the molten pattern stays put while the window glides
   over it — the colours FLOW THROUGH the thumb (warm amber "Shift" → cool violet
   "Day"). During the spring the window squashes/stretches and glows with speed.
   Idle = perfectly still (no idle animation). This block is LAST → it wins.
   ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

body.view-kpi-mode .kpi-flow-mode-control {
  --fg-foil-pos: var(--fg-pp, calc(8% + var(--flow-mode-index, 0) * 84%));
  cursor: pointer;
  touch-action: manipulation;
}

